            <div xml:id="d495">

                <pb facs="0459" n="377" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg377"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/559.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Mexican
                    Ambassador.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-12-19"><hi rendition="#italic">December 19,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 367.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your excellency’s note, No. 422, of the 10th instant, transmitting
                    clippings <pb facs="0460" n="378" xml:id="pg378"/> from the San Antonio Light
                    and Gazette, of the 20th and 21st ultimo, respectively, which, you state, show
                    the character of the acts of Francisco I. Madero.</p>
                <p>In reply I have the honor to state that a copy of your excellency’s note,
                    together with its inclosures, has been sent to the Attorney General for his
                    information.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">P. C. Knox.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
